1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,900
IELTS OS is a complete IELTS study system, not a speaking-only prototype. Listening, Reading, Writing, and Speaking keep their own real practice workflows, while one private AI coach connects the evidence across all four skills.

2
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:35,600
The learner still has a daily plan, practice centre, mistake review, vocabulary, and all four IELTS skills. The AI page does not replace those workflows. It reads the results they produce. Four subject coaches share the same local memory, so a correction in one session can influence the next plan instead of disappearing in a separate feature.

3
00:00:35,600 --> 00:01:06,300
Here the learner completes an actual Listening notes-completion exercise. The app scores the objective answers locally and preserves every mistake with its evidence sentence. Then the Listening coach reads only that score, the mismatches, and prior learning memory. A verified Radeon Cloud inference completed during submission validation; this recording replays that result to avoid free-tier queue variance. The result identifies one priority, cites the supplied evidence, and gives a five-minute drill. No invented Band score is allowed.

4
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:28,300
Reading keeps the article, question set, timer, evidence location, and hint history. The learner answers the questions and submits the attempt. The review distinguishes independent answers from answers completed with a hint. The AI receives that distinction and the verified evidence sentence, then returns a focused solving path and the next short drill instead of generic reading advice.

5
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:50,500
Writing starts with a real prompt and editable draft. Local checks provide immediate word count, paragraph, and connector evidence even if the model is unavailable. The AI then reviews the saved essay, links its feedback to earlier weaknesses, proposes a stronger sentence, and stores the correction as the Writing coach record. The learner can revise the same draft and compare versions.

6
00:01:50,500 --> 00:02:16,200
Speaking uses an immersive English Live mode. The cloud moves through listening, thinking, and speaking states while the Radeon model gives one natural follow-up question. Ending the session creates a conversation summary, a transcript-based review of coherence, vocabulary, and grammar, a stronger sample answer, and the next drill. Pronunciation remains explicitly unscored until an audio-capable local model provides real evidence.

7
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:37,700
Now the private agent sees the four subject reviews together. A planning request calls the local learning-memory and study-status tools. The visible trace shows exactly which private records were used. The final plan is prioritized: it does not assign equal work to every skill, and every task explains the learner evidence behind it. The answer is stored for the next session.

8
00:02:37,700 --> 00:03:00,100
The app talks to one OpenAI-compatible local server. This submission uses Qwen on AMD Radeon Cloud for development and measured inference. Changing one endpoint switches the same agent to Ollama or vLLM on a local Radeon ROCm machine. Personal documents and recordings stay on the device. The learning loop is practice, diagnose, remember, plan, and train again.
